simplified to just setting this to `rule_edge_end_outset`"],["20ab07f6_77705a00",84,-1,1,"nit: missing punctuation"],["29101f22_e461543e",85,-1,1,"nit: I'd add an extra line between each animation var (so one above animation2, one above animation3, and one above animation4) just to make it slightly easier to read"],["3220082e_33bd54eb",82,-1,1,"nit: this could also be `edge_end_value ? edge_end_value : edge_start_value;`"],["368b809c_e4705af4",59,-1,1,"nit: I'd maybe make these all different values to make it obvious they are getting set to each area correctly And I might even add the edge start here too with yet another value to make it clear that…"],["433263a9_faadf35c",53,-1,0,"This one can likely get it from geometry itself. Can is_column_gap, too (maybe not?)"],["4fc60722_26482cf6",82,-1,1,"nit: \"there must be at least\""],["563c89d9_729256c4",82,-1,1,"nit: I'd maybe rephrase to something like \"At least one column rule edge value is needed.\""],["82892834_2c3604a1",53,-1,1,"Since this is now somewhat complex to calculate, I wonder if we should add some helpers to either the gap decorations utils or in the gap geometry to get these values. Maybe one method for the start…"],["89b042ab_cd7df2a8",86,-1,1,"nit: extra line not needed"],["8b869961_e7d4c254",87,-1,1,"Would be interesting to have a positive -end- outset for these fragmentation ones, as well"],["8e6a4735_35b5a2aa",82,-1,1,"The one downside of this is that if another one of these types is added, we may miss adding it here, since we have a default return. Would it make sense to just add cases for the new ones and have…"],["afa3481a_7b156880",53,-1,0,"nit: can we make this one a TODO instead?"],["b0b3addc_f89491b1",82,-1,1,"nit: `consumed_slash`"],["f1b05163_821a1309",2,-1,1,"nit: these can be moved up for alphabetical purposes above kCx"],["f746e3fc_44e25835",82,-1,1,"I wonder if we need both of these, or if we can simplify to just use one set of these?"],["f79b29af_d2bc4737",67,-1,1,"nit: extra spaces not needed"]],0,286],[7107409,20396,581,7.836,6.299,[[1,0.772,51,449],[0,0.228,76,132]],[["649b3fc1_b6d92a7b",88,-1,1,"Same comment as the columns change about setting these to different values (same with other files)"],["79c94821_b4bc338a",68,-1,1,"nit: to keep these with their pairs, we may want to reorder like so: ``` case CSSPropertyID::kColumnRule: ... case CSSPropertyID::kRowRule: ... case CSSPropertyID::kColumnRuleOutset: ... case…"],["e9c1ed36_80caabba",89,-1,1,"Same comment from the columns change about adding an extra line between each animation variable"]],0,287],[7108238,20397,402,4.911,3.884,[[1,0.502,52,201],[0,0.498,77,201]],[["b3a04e0b_53841ec3",79,-2,1,"It looks like this should go below `kRuleColor`"],["b5fbc021_65c0f8ae",3,-2,0,"Maybe a dumb question, but can shorthands be used here as the longhands of rule-outset? I assume not, but would make it slightly simpler if that were possible"],["dc033821_9cbf7764",67,-2,1,"Since we use different test cases for the bidirectional properties, I think it would be a bit cleaner to move that one to its own test instead"],["240a1849_7ca191d1",90,-1,1,"nit: missing extra line at the end of the test"],["34f5c75b_67b00ad2",91,-1,1,"Same here"],["39282aa9_57b01ab5",92,-1,1,"Same here"],["b9941c13_0c7242bb",93,-1,1,"Was this meant to still be commented out?"]],0,288],[7125761,20402,240,2.983,2.275,[[0,0.94,78,228],[1,0.06,53,12]],[["01e29a76_d0087fc7",52,-3,1,"\"in that case\" Although, curious why (perhaps adding more details as mentioned above for why when there is a spanner there are 3 will help make that clearer)"],["1827d7ac_5ddeb76a",49,-3,1,"This could probably use a comment"],["266efa88_66a89eb7",52,-3,0,"Can you remind me why there is 3 when adjacent to a spanner?"],["38eaadcb_d1b7401a",49,-3,1,"This should be guaranteed by the if-statement above, so we can either remove this one, or if we should never get in this state to begin with, remove it from the if-statement above And then whichever…"],["3de3fdea_87215364",49,-3,1,"nit: extra lines after \"break\" shouldn't be needed (here or below)"],["456835b9_55e5edd8",52,-3,1,"nit: this looks like it can be re-wrapped"],["4c7bc365_34266746",49,-3,1,"Is anything here multicol specific? If not, would it make sense for this to live in the gap geometry class instead?"],["53c58d2c_2af862cb",53,-3,0,"Just to double check, the intersection state is being used for other things elsewhere? Otherwise, if it is just this, it would seem like multicol is still being interpreted as always being at the edge"],["579bceb9_d278090d",49,-3,0,"Is it possible for something to have an \"end\" state before \"start\" is set? If not, would it maybe make sense as a CHECK_NE?"],["7c9b37f0_b9266a43",52,-3,1,"nit: I'd put this part in parens (i.e. \"All (2 or 3) intersections..\""],["a356033d_f3d4dbb9",49,-3,0,"Out of curiosity, can you remind me how other layout types are doing this? I don't recall any doing this sort of updating after the fact. Is this because of spanners etc?"],["ac6a9319_0d1a2f6b",4,-3,0,"Why was this needed to be changed in this CL as opposed to a column-wrap CL? Did it have something to do with the interaction with edge states that made it all mixed up?"],["e1358ce2_c0b6e21d",49,-3,0,"Won't we get here if main_gaps_.back().HasCrossGapsBefore() is not true, but this are main gaps? Or can that never happen?"],["f4a20d45_ff1b83a1",53,-3,1,"This might make sense as a TODO since it is still an open question"],["fda8376f_8c6e9d04",49,-3,0,"Is there any way to know these edge states when we are adding things earlier so that we don't have to update them at the end? A comment here may help in explaining"],["b1eacfd3_263f3f1f",42,-1,0,"If we moved this method to main_gaps.h would we need to pass this in?"]],0,289],[7127743,20402,1452,7.883,6.167,[[1,0.548,54,782],[0,0.422,79,628],[2,0.015,8,22],[3,0.015,9,22]],[["01f88889_4d4696f2",2,-3,1,"Where is ColumnRuleOutset/Inset? Is that one not added yet?"],["2d39f54e_a4020963",4,-3,1,"nit: \"will require\""],["438f44b6_33b1adf9",4,-3,1,"nit: \"changes\""],["95139b56_715fcf2a",4,-3,1,"nit: \"Although\""]],0,290],[7127964,20402,0,0.12,0.081,[[1,1.0,55,914]],[],0,291],[7131883,20403,444,4.911,3.884,[[1,0.962,56,428],[0,0.038,80,16]],[],0,292],[7138738,20403,215,2.983,2.275,[[0,81]],[["9b252c3e_56e41876",94,0,1,"These look like they are included in the .h. Is this needed here, or should we remove from .h?"]],0,293],[7169205,20410,309,4.911,3.884,[[1,57]],[],0,294],[7170183,20411,313,4.911,3.884,[[0,1.0,82,307]],[["17f1b8dd_365e77f9",48,-1,0,"Not sure if it's within the scope of this CL, but what do you think of having a Generator class, that abstracts this logic? Instead of doing this like \"functionally\" ..."],["4090a92c_49366f05",52,0,1,"Since we already alter the reference of intersections, why do we need to return here?"],["655fdc0a_2c9af53a",48,0,1,"Same comment as above"],["790c4f0b_f6560c97",48,0,1,"nit: \"the main gap at `gap_index`\"? (not sure if that's accurate since wasn't sure what \"this\" referred to here)"],["87839151_f2e764a9",48,0,1,"nit: \"This includes...\""],["abf00774_693c2623",48,0,1,"Is this bullet separate from the first (i.e. that it implies we are adding different types of gaps based on each bullet, or are they talking about the same ones?) If these aren't disjoint, I'd…"],["b0fee27e_733bb5c2",48,0,1,"\", which includes:\""],["cbe2e779_659fa90f",48,0,1,"I'd suggest adding comments for all of these new ones (particularly to note the out param etc)"],["f97020bf_6cf76d3e",52,0,1,"nit: extra ;"],["fab17cf9_7f2fcc93",52,0,1,"Same with the rest of these, do we need to return, or just use the existing out param?"]],0,295],[7169664,20412,17,0.518,0.377,[[0,83]],[["f2383164_a008c3a2",52,0,1,"I think Alison had made a point to have this as an iterator to achieve O(1) time since they are somewhat accessed in order. So I'll leave that in the TODO."]],0,296],[7185447,20414,2304,7.883,6.167,[[5,0]],[],0,297],[7219490,20426,75,1.637,1.223,[[1,0.835